  "question": {
    "text": "Two beams of light having intensities&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>I</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mi>I</mi></math>, interfere to produce a fringe pattern on a screen. The phase difference between the beams is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac bevelled=\"true\"><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>,&nbsp;at a point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> and <math> <mrow> <mi>π</mi> </mrow> </math>,&nbsp;at a point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>. The difference between the resultant intensities at&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> is",
